Body:
> thank you for finding this, we are merging fixes today and releasing

tnx for the quick work @thdxr. I passed this by the agent that found the original issue, and it said that [parts are still loaded by ID](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/blob/fe82a1b6ca4f535beb973b0867017e3f639f85ed/packages/opencode/src/session/message-v2.ts#L98-L108). 

From what I understand, this means that message generated during the wrap time can have their parts messed up. E.g. if a thinking block is before the wrap, and the tool call / text after. 

This fails rn:

```
import { expect, test } from "bun:test"
import { Database } from "@opencode-ai/core/database/database"
import { PartTable } from "@opencode-ai/core/session/sql"
import { Effect } from "effect"
import { MessageV2 } from "../../src/session/message-v2"
import { MessageID, PartID, SessionID } from "../../src/session/schema"

test("loads parts chronologically across the timestamp wrap", async () => {
  const messageID = MessageID.make("msg_repro")
  const sessionID = SessionID.make("ses_repro")
  const before = PartID.make("prt_fffffffff001AAAAAAAAAAAAAA")
  const after = PartID.make("prt_000000000001BBBBBBBBBBBBBB")

  const program = Effect.gen(function* () {
    const { db } = yield* Database.Service
    yield* db.run("PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF")
    yield* db.insert(PartTable).values([
      {
        id: before,
        message_id: messageID,
        session_id: sessionID,
        time_created: 1_786_706_395_135,
        time_updated: 1_786_706_395_135,
        data: { type: "text", text: "before" },
      },
      {
        id: after,
        message_id: messageID,
        session_id: sessionID,
        time_created: 1_786_706_395_136,
        time_updated: 1_786_706_395_136,
        data: { type: "text", text: "after" },
      },
    ])

    return yield* MessageV2.parts(messageID)
  })

  const parts = await Effect.runPromise(
    program.pipe(Effect.provide(Database.layerFromPath(":memory:"))),
  )

  expect(parts.map((part) => part.id)).toEqual([before, after])
})
```

This fix seems to solve it 

```
.orderBy(PartTable.message_id, PartTable.time_created, PartTable.id)
.orderBy(PartTable.time_created, PartTable.id)
```

Does this check out?
